        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eeaed7bb-ed47-5552-993c-e4ee6d64d6a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacques Demy, Paul Sloane, Cecil B. DeMille, Stepin Fetchit, Cary Grant, Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, Walter Brennan\n- Films: The Umbrellas of Cherbourg, The Young Girls of Rochefort, Hearts in Dixie, The Woman Accused, The Texans, Break of Day, Eve's Leaves\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Sloane was born on April 19, 1893, and he became a writer and film director.\n- Paul Sloane directed 26 films from 1925 to 1952 and wrote or co-wrote 35 films.\n- The film Eve's Leaves was directed by Paul Sloane and was produced and distributed by Cecil B. DeMille.\n- Paul Sloane's films include Hearts in Dixie (1929), which featured Stepin Fetchit.\n- Paul Sloane's films include The Woman Accused (1933), which featured Cary Grant.\n- Paul Sloane directed The Texans, which featured Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, and Walter Brennan.\n- Jacques Demy directed The Umbrellas of Cherbourg in 1964 and The Young Girls of Rochefort in 1967, and he is best known for these two musicals.\n- Break of Day was adapted into a 1980 film directed by Jacques Demy.\n- Paul Sloane died on November 15, 1963.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "76d64449-f6f4-55de-bfae-8a6a54a7ff7a",
        "text": "Page: Jacques Demy. Sentence: He is best known for the two musicals he directed in the mid-1960s: \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\" (1964) and \"The Young Girls of Rochefort\" (1967).\nPage: Paul Sloane (director). Sentence: Paul Sloane (April 19, 1893 – November 15, 1963) was a writer and film director who directed 26 films from 1925 to 1952, and wrote or co-wrote 35 films.\nPage: Paul Sloane (director). Sentence: His movies include \"Hearts in Dixie\" (1929) with Stepin Fetchit, \"The Woman Accused\" (1933) with Cary Grant, and \"The Texans\" with Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott and Walter Brennan.\nPage: Break of Day. Sentence: It was adapted into a 1980 film directed by Jacques Demy.\nPage: Eve's Leaves. Sentence: The film was produced and distributed by Cecil B. DeMille and directed by Paul Sloane.",
